    "source": "",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A slab of scribed steel and hex-glyph plate that projects a small reality-stabilizing null field. The broken, corrupted, please-stop-hitting-yourself things of the Qliphoth can't get a grip on what stands behind it. Heavy. Slow. Worth it.</p><p><strong>Null Field.</strong> Resists qliphothic damage and, while braced, extends the steadying field to one adjacent ally (they ignore Compelled until they move away).</p><hr><p><strong>⚙️ Mechanical Effects</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor:</strong> Shield</p></li><li><p><strong>Defense:</strong> Guard +3, Evasion -1, Resolve +1</p></li><li><p><strong>Requires:</strong> Bracing (trained)</p></li><li><p><strong>Resistance:</strong> Qliphothic</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier:</strong> III</p></li><li><p><strong>Cost:</strong> 630 Nonlethal marks</p></li></ul>",
